### 6.2 Policy Improvement with Steered Video World Model Imaginations

π0.5\pi_{0.5}

Setup. We study whether StressDream can improve a robotic policy through steered WM imaginations, promoting robust actions that remain successful over the distribution of outcomes. We consider improving a behavior-cloning policy, the Vision-Language-Action (VLA) model π0.5\pi\_{0.5} [[57](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2606.00267v1#bib.bib67)], with action evaluation in WM imaginations. Specifically, we fine-tune π0.5\pi\_{0.5}-droid with 4040 successful demonstrations per task using a weighted regression objective [[41](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2606.00267v1#bib.bib109)], and compare two settings: Nominal π0.5FT\pi\_{0.5}^{\mathrm{FT}}, which assigns a uniform weight of 1.01.0 to all trajectories, and Robust π0.5FT\pi\_{0.5}^{\mathrm{FT}}, which assigns weight 1.01.0 to trajectories that remain successful under steering toward task failures and weight 0.10.1 to trajectories that fail in steered imaginations. This encourages robust actions whose plausible outcome distribution does not include failures, while downweighting risky actions that can fail.

